<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithms and proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of no dominant strategy</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Claim.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">No agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> in the game <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math> has a dominant strategy.</em></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of agents, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of goods.
For each agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math> and good <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\in\mathbf{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\in\mathbf{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is a valuation <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{ig}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{ig}\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The (feasible) allocations are given by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{ig}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{ig}</annotation></semantics></math>, the amount of good <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> allocated to agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">welfare</span> of agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\;=\;\sum_{g\in\mathbf{G}}\,v_{ig}\,a_{ig}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\;=\;\sum_{g\in\mathbf{G}}\,v_{ig}\,a_{ig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">total social welfare</span> is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\;=\;\sum_{i\in\mathbf{I}}\,w_{i}\;=\;\sum_{i\in\mathbf{I}}\sum_{g\in\mathbf{G}}v_{ig}\,a_{ig}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐆</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\;=\;\sum_{i\in\mathbf{I}}\,w_{i}\;=\;\sum_{i\in\mathbf{I}}\sum_{g\in\mathbf{G}}v_{ig}\,a_{ig}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Let each agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> have a strategy space <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. A (pure) strategy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a complete description of agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s behavior in the market (e.g., how they propose, reject, accept, etc.).
We write <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}</annotation></semantics></math> for a strategy profile of all agents other than <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s_{i},\mathbf{s}_{-i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s_{i},\mathbf{s}_{-i})</annotation></semantics></math> denote agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s resulting payoff (or final utility/welfare) under strategy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> against opponents’ strategies <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A strategy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">dominant</span> for agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> if, for <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all</span> <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}\in\mathcal{S}_{-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}\in\mathcal{S}_{-i}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\;\;\geq\;\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\quad\text{for all }s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.560em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\;\;\geq\;\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\quad\text{for all }s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">In other words, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees the highest possible utility for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, irrespective of what other players do.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume, by way of contradiction, that there exists a dominant strategy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for some agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of dominance, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\;\geq\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\quad\text{for all }s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}_{i}\text{ and for all }\mathbf{s}_{-i}\in\mathcal{S}_{-i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\;\geq\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i},\mathbf{s}_{-i}\bigr)\quad\text{for all }s_{i}\in\mathcal{S}_{i}\text{ and for all }\mathbf{s}_{-i}\in\mathcal{S}_{-i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Construct two different scenarios of other agents’ strategies and valuations, denoted by <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>. These scenarios can differ in 1) how other agents value the goods <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{v_{jg}:j\neq i\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{v_{jg}:j\neq i\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and 2) the demands or offers they make (i.e. how <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}</annotation></semantics></math> translates into allocations <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{jg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{jg}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In scenario <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose the other agents are willing to trade or allocate a certain good <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> to agent <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> only if <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> offers a high price or concedes in some manner. A specialized alternative strategy <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> (instead of <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) might yield a strictly higher payoff if <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> trades aggressively for <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In scenario <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose the others behave differently (e.g., they no longer place much value on <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> but highly value some other good). Now a different specialized strategy <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> might yield a strictly higher payoff (because trading strategy for <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in scenario <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is no longer beneficial here).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contradiction of dominance:</span> Because scenarios <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> are both feasible profiles of opponents’ behavior (<math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>), there is no single strategy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> that can simultaneously guarantee at least as high a payoff as both <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> across those distinct opponent profiles. Formally,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exists\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}:u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{A},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}\bigr)\;&gt;\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}\bigr),\quad\text{and}\quad\exists\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}:u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{B},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}\bigr)\;&gt;\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∃</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exists\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}:u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{A},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}\bigr)\;&gt;\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}\bigr),\quad\text{and}\quad\exists\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}:u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{B},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}\bigr)\;&gt;\;u_{i}\bigl(s_{i}^{*},\,\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This contradicts the definition of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> as a dominant strategy.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Because the above argument does not rely on any special assumption beyond the existence of at least two different plausible profiles <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>A</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐬</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}_{-i}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we conclude that no strategy for agent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> can be dominant. Since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> was arbitrary, no agent in the game has a dominant strategy. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Empirical computation of increasing game complexity</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Claim.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">The decision space increases quadratically as the number of chip colors increases.</em></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This is a simple consequence that in games with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> different colors of chips, there are <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{k}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{k}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> possible pairs of chips to transact. Since the distribution of opponents’ valuations is symmetric across chips (except the green numeraire chip), each proposer must consider <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(k^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(k^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> different feasible trades. Indeed, if we empirically compute the expected number of myopically rational trades<span id="footnote15" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">15</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">15</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">15</span>
                
                
                
              We define a myopically rational trade to be one where the proposer gains surplus and assigns some probability that at least one opponent would gain surplus by accepting the trade.</span></span></span> in the starting configuration of the 2, 3, and 4-chip game, we arrive at 37.1, 120.7, 250.7 respectively. That is the 3-chip game has approximately <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as many myopically rational trades in expectation as the 2-chip game, and the 4-chip game has approximately <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{4}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{4}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. This approximation becomes more exact as the number of chips increases due to the reduced relative impact of the numeraire.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Multi-agent trading algorithm with Bayesian learning</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Multi-agent Trading Algorithm with Bayesian Learning</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Inputs:</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>: set of players

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐆</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{G}</annotation></semantics></math>: set of goods

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
